<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><%- include("partials/head") %><title>Signing in for the first time — Atlas</title></head>
<body>
<div class="top"><b>ATLAS PAYROLL</b><span class="spacer"></span><a href="/login">Sign in</a></div>
<main>
  <h1>Signing in for the first time</h1>
  <div class="panel">
    <p>People Ops creates your Atlas account on your first day. You do not pick your
    own password — IT issues a temporary one built from a fixed pattern:</p>
    <p><code>Atlas</code> + the year you joined + <code>!</code></p>
    <p class="muted">Example: someone who joined in 2023 starts on <code>Atlas2023!</code></p>
    <p>Change it under <em>Profile &rarr; Security</em> within fourteen days of your start
    date. Your start date is shown in the people directory.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="panel">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0">Sign-in codes</h3>
    <p>Atlas mails a four-digit code every time you sign in. Codes are valid for the
    length of the sign-in attempt. If one does not arrive, use <em>Send another
    code</em> as many times as you need — earlier codes keep working, so you can
    type whichever one reaches you first.</p>
  </div>
</main>
</body></html>
